description:
FOUND s494p (Opus, 2026-09-25) by member 4's retaining-site census (task #2098 === THE GENERAL-PATH CENSUS ===).  PRE-EXISTING (3e8bff3e).

Reproducer (scratch/s494p/memfh.pl in the s494p worktree):
    my $buf = ""; open my $fh, ">", \$buf or die; print $fh "a";
    my $copy = $buf; my @arr = ($buf); my %h = (k => $buf); my %kk; $kk{$buf} = 1;
    print $fh "b"; close $fh;
    print "[$copy] [$arr[0]] [$h{k}] [", join(",", keys %kk), "] ", (exists $kk{"a"} ? "key-a" : "no-key-a"), " [$buf]\n";
perl:  [a] [a] [a] [a] key-a [ab]
PCL:   [ab] [ab] [ab] [ab] no-key-a [ab]

WHY: %p-open-memory stores an ADJUSTABLE fill-pointer string (%p-fresh-adjustable-string) in the target box and the Gray stream (%psos-buf) appends to it IN PLACE.  Every value copy in the runtime shares string objects (to-string returns the string itself; box-set's fast path stores it; %p-storable-raw parks it raw in an array slot; a hash store uses it as the KEY of an `equal` table), so the mutation reaches every copy — and a mutated key breaks the table's hashing.  This is exactly the OWNERSHIP invariant member 4 of s494p sizes for a general in-place `.=`: the SHARED-STRINGS note above *p-small-fixnum-strings* ("nothing writes into a plain simple-string it did not make") is violated today by this one producer.
FIX SHAPES (both measured in #2098's census): (a) snapshot at the retaining chokepoints — box-set's two store arms, %p-storable-raw, the array-store copy arm, ONE hash-key coercion helper (today ~32 `to-string` key sites), bless's class name — which the general `.=` would need anyway; (b) local to this producer: keep the stream's buffer PRIVATE and snapshot into the box on each write — O(length) per print, i.e. quadratic for the capture-output idiom, so (a) is the real fix.  BAR: the reproducer + io/ companion (io/perlio_open.t, io/print.t, op/sprintf.t use in-memory handles) + sweep.
